<Layout title="slot.advance — suprlab"><div class="wrap"><header class="article-head"><a class="eyebrow" href={`${base}#projects`}>SUPRLAB / SELECTED PROJECTS</a><h1>slot.advance</h1><p>GBA, with intention. A focused build of slot for the Anbernic RG SP (2026).</p><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/slowphase/slot.advance">Repository</a><a href="https://github.com/slowphase/slot.advance/releases">Releases</a><a href="https://github.com/slowphase/slot.advance/blob/main/documentation/user-guide.md">User guide</a></div></header><img class="article-image" src={`${base}projects/slot-advance.webp`} alt="slot.advance running on the Anbernic RG SP"/><article class="prose project-prose"><h2>Built around the way you play.</h2><p>Close the lid and your game waits in memory. Open it and carry on. slot.advance takes slot’s minimal design and shapes it around Game Boy Advance games on one device: the Anbernic RG SP (2026), with its 720 × 480 display.</p><h2>The useful little details</h2><ul><li>Real hardware sleep and instant resume.</li><li>Optional Wi-Fi, off by default.</li><li>Syncthing for saves and states across your devices.</li><li>RetroAchievements with offline progress.</li><li>A cartridge shelf, favourites and five save states per game.</li></ul><p>This build supports the RG SP (2026) only. For the older RG35XX SP or other devices, see upstream slot.</p><h2>Built on good work</h2><p>slot.advance is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/BrandonKowalski/slot">slot by Brandon T. Kowalski</a>. The carousel, cartridge shelf, save-state switcher, link play and much of the interface come from his work.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/slowphase/slot.advance">See the project, installation instructions and full credits on GitHub.</a></p></article></div></Layout>
